Elisp written for Emacs 24 and later reaches for defvar-local, alist-get,
string-trim, string-empty-p, when-let, seq-filter and, on Emacs 21, dolist
and delete-dups.  This package defines each of them only when the running
Emacs does not have it, so a package that needs them can require
emacs-compat and keep the sources it uses everywhere else.

Emacs 20 needs devel/emacs20-compat, which has more to do; XEmacs needs
devel/xemacs-compat.
